From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmime: PlaySegmentEx QUEUE / TIMESIG_ALWAYS / VALID_START / INVALIDATE_PRI flags and the from argument

IDirectMusicPerformance8::PlaySegmentEx: the flags and the "from" argument.

- DMUS_SEGF_QUEUE: a primary segment starts when the last primary segment
  state queued before it ends (the start time is ignored); with nothing
  queued it starts at once. Secondary segments ignore the flag.
- DMUS_SEGF_MARKER / DMUS_SEGF_SEGMENTEND resolve the start time to the next
  marker / the end of the primary segment (patch 2914).
- DMUS_SEGF_TIMESIG_ALWAYS: grid, beat and measure boundaries are resolved
  (4/4 by default) even when no primary segment plays.
- DMUS_SEGF_VALID_START_{TICK,GRID,BEAT,MEASURE}: the segment state starts
  at the first valid start point (GUID_Valid_Start_Time of the marker track)
  at or after the segment's start point which is on one of the asked for
  boundaries of the segment's time signature; with none it starts at the
  start point. DMUS_SEGF_ALIGN is accepted: the start point is what is put
  on the resolved boundary, which is what the state does anyway.
- DMUS_SEGF_INVALIDATE_PRI: the tracks of the primary segment play again
  from the start time of the new segment (DMUS_TRACKF_SEEK | DIRTY), as
  Invalidate does. DMUS_SEGF_NOINVALIDATE and DMUS_SEGF_USE_AUDIOPATH are
  accepted (the audio path argument is used when it is given).
- from: a segment state, or an audio path whose segment states, are stopped
  at the start time of the new segment (Stop / StopEx of patch 2914: at once
  when that time has come). Anything else is E_INVALIDARG.
